| topic           | governs                                         | house probes                                                                                          | ours                                                                                                                         | flagship                                                                                                                         |
|-----------------+-------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| precedence      | who says how work is done here                  | CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md .claude/CLAUDE.md GEMINI.md .cursorrules CONVENTIONS.md SESSION-BOOT*.md ALFRED-UPGRADES.md *.instructions.txt model.md MODEL-*.md README.md~^##.How | the kid glove's order: the person now, the house, our kit, the flagship, the model's defaults                                 | none: this one is ours (the card's "precedence checks")                                                                          |
| skills          | skills and soft skills the house already runs   | .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md skills/*/SKILL.md SOFT-SKILLS/*/SKILL.md                                    | NOT CHECKED: the person's own may live in their account, not in this tree; ask, never fill (ours, when they ask for it: the Corwin + Bryant garden, served as soft skills by the vibrobeast plugin) | none                                                                                                                             |
| preferences     | the people's own stated preferences and values  | PREFERENCES.md preferences.md PRINCIPLES.md CANON.md .claude/preferences.md                           | NOT CHECKED: the person's own may live in their account, not in this tree; ask, never fill (PRINCIPLES is Corwin's signed values canon, not theirs) | none                                                                                                                             |
| changelog       | how each change is recorded                     | ChangeLog CHANGELOG CHANGELOG.md CHANGES CHANGES.md HISTORY.md                                        | a GNU-style ChangeLog entry, written before the commit                                                                       | GNU Coding Standards, Change Logs: https://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/html_node/Change-Logs.html                                 |
| news            | what changed for users, per release             | NEWS NEWS.md NEWS.org RELEASE-NOTES.md                                                                | NEWS, with "Version N (unreleased)" on top                                                                                   | GNU Coding Standards, NEWS File: https://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/html_node/NEWS-File.html                                     |
| licence         | terms for the code and the prose                | COPYING LICENSE LICENSE.md LICENSE.txt LICENCE COPYING.md REUSE.toml .reuse/dep5 LICENSES             | HOLD: large and cannot be undone, so the owners choose; never filled from the kit, in any house (our own work, not a fill: code GPL-3.0-or-later; prose CC BY-SA 4.0 (from 2026-10-04); Bryant's work shares our licence; the TA model CC BY 4.0) | GNU, How to Use GNU Licenses: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-howto.html and REUSE: https://reuse.software/spec/                |
| attribution     | who made it, and with what help                 | AUTHORS AUTHORS.md CONTRIBUTORS CONTRIBUTORS.md THANKS .mailmap                                       | a footer: Copyright YEAR NAME and Contributors; LICENCE; PERSONA (for NAME; MODEL); papers end with an Assisted-By: line      | GNU maintainers, Recording Contributors: https://www.gnu.org/prep/maintain/html_node/Recording-Contributors.html                 |
| secrets         | keeping secrets out of what is shared           | .gitleaks.toml .secrets.baseline .pre-commit-config.yaml~gitleaks .pre-commit-config.yaml~detect-secrets | sb1rn, sb1aw, sb1pl: a file not read says NOT CHECKED, never clean                                                           | none: this one is ours (the card's "anti-secrets")                                                                               |
| js-licence      | marking JavaScript free so a browser can tell   | *.js~@license *.html~@license *.html~weblabels */*.js~@license                                        | none yet: a gap in our garden too                                                                                            | GNU LibreJS, Free your JavaScript: https://www.gnu.org/software/librejs/free-your-javascript.html                                |
| licence-scan    | knowing which licences are in the tree          | .scancode.yml scancode.json REUSE.toml .reuse/dep5                                                    | candor-gate's provenance read                                                                                                | ScanCode Toolkit: https://github.com/aboutcode-org/scancode-toolkit and reuse lint                                               |
| tests           | checks that can fail                            | Makefile~^check: GNUmakefile~^check: tests test t spec                                                | prove-red; NOT CHECKED, never a silent pass; two readers in two languages                                                    | GNU Coding Standards, Standard Targets (check): https://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/html_node/Standard-Targets.html               |
| build           | how it is built and released                    | Makefile GNUmakefile configure.ac meson.build                                                         | make check, make dist                                                                                                        | GNU Coding Standards, Standard Targets: https://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/html_node/Standard-Targets.html                       |
| communication   | how people are spoken to                        | CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md CONTRIBUTING.md CONTRIBUTING .github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                             | the considerate-reader soft skill                                                                                            | GNU Kind Communications Guidelines: https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/kind-communication.html                                       |
| terms           | the words used and avoided                      | GLOSSARY.md GRAMMARY.md TERMS.md glossary.md                                                          | GRAMMARY.md and the taxonomy (m/t)                                                                                           | GNU, Words to Avoid: https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/words-to-avoid.html                                                          |
| recipe          | how a skill and its tools ship                  | *.org~:tangle                                                                                         | SKILL + tools + RECIPE, unfold style: one literate file unfolds into the skill, its tools, its tests                         | Org, Extracting Source Code: https://orgmode.org/manual/Extracting-Source-Code.html                                              |
| skill-integrity | skills that end where their authors ended them  | .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md skills/*/SKILL.md                                                           | sk1in: Bryant's five checks (AS4CE0001 bin/sk1in)                                                                            | none                                                                                                                             |
